# Caddyfile for the Railway static site (see Railway's SPA guide).
# Railway terminates TLS at the edge, so Caddy only serves plain HTTP
# on the injected $PORT. The site is a Vite SPA: serve dist/, fall back
# to index.html for client-side routes.
#
# /indexer/* is reverse-proxied to the marketplace indexer on the Vultr
# server. The browser only ever talks HTTPS to Railway, so this avoids
# the mixed-content block that stops an HTTPS page fetching the
# plain-HTTP indexer directly. handle_path strips the /indexer prefix,
# so /indexer/status reaches the indexer as /status.
:{$PORT:3000} {
	handle_path /indexer/* {
		reverse_proxy http://64.177.54.210:3001
	}

	handle {
		root * dist
		encode gzip
		file_server
		try_files {path} /index.html
	}
}
